abstract: "M³-AVM (Multimodal Multi-Model Abstract Virtual Machine) is a deterministic virtual machine prototype in Rust for sparse event-driven tensor computation: ISA v1.12 with 32-byte instructions (control/thinking loop 0x00-0x0F, GEMV 0x10-0x12, Mamba/SSM and audio codec 0x13-0x19, local cluster 0x1A-0x1D, GATHER 0x1F / DISTANCE 0x23 / RANK1_UPDATE 0x24 / FOREST 0x22 / DENOISE 0x21 / ODE 0x25 / SPIKE 0x20 / CONV 0x1E, memory/arena 0x26-0x29, MEMCPY/MEMSET 0x2A-0x2B, PREFETCH/RESHAPE/CONCAT 0x2C/0x2D/0x2F, CAST/QUANTIZE/DEQUANT 0x67-0x69, shape ops 0x30-0x37, SOFTMAX/activations 0x3C-0x43, KV_COMPRESS/FLASH_ATTN/ATTN_SPARSE 0x39-0x3B, audio DSP 0x45-0x49, KV_TRUNCATE 0x38, SLICE 0x2E, RNG/hash 0x60-0x66, telemetry/scheduler 0x6A-0x77, LOADI/MOV 0x78-0x79, ADD_IMM/SUB_IMM/STEPS 0x7A-0x7C, NOP 0xFF), strict unknown-token rejection in the assembler, strict-priority scheduler (Red > Blue > Green) with absolute deadlines, CoW snapshot/rollback (FORK/ABORT) with monotonic version counter and retention window, CSR sparse tensors, Q4_K fused AVX2 matvec, GGUF mmap inference with per-layer KV cache, criterion benches for the hybrid opcodes, and Lean 4 proofs (SSM, rollback, windowed error). Distributed transport and remaining universal-AI waves are frozen/reserved future work (see docs/ESPEC.md normative, docs/ESPEC-V2.md draft)."
keywords:
  - virtual-machine
  - tensor
  - sparse-computation
